==Swedish==
[[File:Ensvensktigerskylt2 djuramossa.jpg|thumb|300px|[[w:En svensk tiger|En svensk '''tiger''']] ["A Swedish '''tiger''' / A Swede '''keeps silent'''" – design from a World War II propaganda campaign, like "{{w|loose lips sink ships}}"] ]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|þighia}}, from {{inh|sv|non|þegja}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*þagjaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|sv|Sv-tiga.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-irr|tiger|teg|tigit|tig}}

# to [[refrain]] from [[saying]] anything, to [[keep]] [[silent]], to [[stay]] [[silent]]
#: {{syn|sv|hålla käften|q=vulgar, offensive in the imperative}}
#: {{ux|sv|Hon '''teg'''|She '''kept quiet'''}}
# {{lb|sv|in "(försöka) tiga ihjäl något/någon" (literally, "(try to) kill something/someone through staying silent")}} to deliberately [[ignore]] (something/someone, to (try to) prevent that thing or person from gaining influence), to give the [[silent treatment]]
#: {{ux|sv|De kommer försöka '''tiga ihjäl''' boken|They will try to '''kill''' the book (containing accusations or the like) '''through silence'''}}
# {{lb|sv|imperative|dated|impolite}} [[be quiet]]!
#: {{syn|sv|håll käften|q1=offensive|käften}}

